    "title": "Low-cost grocery option ALDI comes to Nicholasville - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Madylin Goins ,\n10 hours ago\nNICHOLASVILLE, Ky. ( FOX 56 ) — Nicholasville shoppers will soon have another low-cost grocery option as ALDI opens a new store on Keene Centre Drive.\nOfficials will cut the ribbon on the Keene Center location at 8:30 a.m. on Thursday, June 25.\nRead more of the latest Kentucky news “At our new Nicholasville ALDI store, customers will see why so many already choose ALDI for their weekly grocery shopping,” said Laura Bauer, regional vice president for ALDI. “As shoppers look to stretch their dollar further, we’re excited to open this new location and bring more people a high-quality grocery selection they want and need at the lowest possible price. “\nThe grocer will be open daily from 9 a.m. to 8 p.m.\nTo celebrate its grand opening, the first 200 customers will receive a gift bag filled with a sampling of ALDI products and a gift card as part of the ALDI Golden Ticket giveaway program.\nLATEST KENTUCKY NEWS: The Nicholasville store’s opening brings ALDI one step closer to its goal of having 3,200 stores by the end of 2028.\nCopyright 2026 Nexstar Media, Inc. All rights reserved. This material may not be published, broadcast, rewritten, or redistributed. For the latest news, weather, sports, and streaming video, head to FOX 56 News.\n4",
